.TH SLERP 1 "October 2026" "slerp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slerp \- thumbnailer and viewer for 3D models, textures, game assets and other graphics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slerp
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B slerp view
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B slerp thumbnail
.I SIZE INPUT OUTPUT
.br
.B slerp render
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR STATE ]
.RB [ \-\-content ]
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.br
.B slerp info
.RB [ \-\-part
.IR PART ]
.I FILE
.br
.B slerp convert
.RB [ \-\-part
.IR PART ]
.RB [ \-\-centre ]
.RB [ \-\-png ]
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.br
.B slerp contents list
.I FILE
.br
.B slerp contents extract
.I FILE
.RI [ ITEM ...]
.B \-\-out
.I DIR
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR FORMAT ]
.RB [ \-\-centre ]
.RB [ \-\-skeleton\-only ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B slerp associate
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B slerp formats
.br
.B slerp helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slerp makes file-manager thumbnails of the files desktops show as generic
icons, and opens them in a viewer: GPU textures (KTX2, DDS, ASTC), 3D models
(glTF, FBX, OBJ, USD, Blender, SketchUp, Maya and many more), Gaussian splats,
point clouds, materials, Quake and Doom levels, 2D game formats, CAD drawings,
documents, and scientific, medical and retro images.
.B slerp formats
lists every format it reads.
.PP
File managers run
.B slerp thumbnail
through the freedesktop thumbnailer file
.IR /usr/share/thumbnailers/slerp.thumbnailer .
The first thumbnail that needs a GPU starts
.BR "slerp helper" ,
which keeps the GPU loaded for later thumbnails and exits after two idle
minutes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR view " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Opens the viewer, on
.I FILE
when given.  With no command at all,
.B slerp
.I FILE
does the same.  A viewer that stayed loaded after its window closed opens the
file at once.  F1 in the viewer lists its keyboard shortcuts.
.TP
.B thumbnail \fISIZE INPUT OUTPUT\fR
Writes a PNG thumbnail of
.I INPUT
no larger than
.I SIZE
pixels to
.IR OUTPUT .
.TP
.B render \fIINPUT OUTPUT\fR
Renders one frame offscreen to a PNG,
.B \-\-size
pixels across (512 by default).
.B \-\-state
replays a view state the viewer copied with Ctrl+Shift+C (camera, clip and
time, morphs, overlays).  Without a state, a file that carries a picture of
itself gives that picture, unless
.B \-\-content
is given.
.TP
.B info \fIFILE\fR
Prints what a file holds.
.B \-\-part
picks one part of a file that holds several, such as a WAD's map.
.TP
.B convert \fIINPUT OUTPUT\fR
Converts any 3D file Slerp opens to GLB.
.B \-\-centre
moves the centre of the scene's box to the origin, and
.B \-\-png
writes every picture as PNG instead of keeping the original files.
.TP
.B contents list \fIFILE\fR
Prints the items inside a file as a tree: an archive's entries, a model's
nodes, meshes, materials, textures and clips, a texture's mips, layers and
faces, a sprite's layers and frames, a document's pages.
.TP
.B contents extract \fIFILE\fR [\fIITEM\fR...] \fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR
Writes the items named (paths, names, folders or globs such as
.BR *.png ;
all of them when none is named) as ordinary files under
.IR DIR ,
never outside it, and never over an existing file unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.B \-\-format
is one of auto, raw, png, exr, wav, mid, wad or glb.
.TP
.B associate
Chooses which formats get Slerp's thumbnails and open in Slerp by default,
and makes the desktop follow.
.B \-\-list
shows every format,
.B \-\-thumbnails on|off
and
.B \-\-default on|off
change the choices for formats, categories or
.BR all ,
.B \-\-apply
applies the saved choices again (run it once per user to enable Slerp's
thumbnails in Dolphin, and after updates), and
.B \-\-reset
undoes every change Slerp made outside its own settings.  Every option takes
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B formats
Prints the table of formats Slerp handles.
.TP
.B helper
Runs the resident thumbnail helper.  It is started on demand; there is no
need to run it by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/slerp/config.jsonc
Settings, all optional: the GPU for thumbnails
.RB ( gpu :
auto, integrated, discrete, software, or part of an adapter's name) and for
the viewer
.RB ( viewerGpu ),
how long the helper and the viewer stay loaded
.RB ( helperIdleSeconds ", " viewerKeepAliveSeconds ),
and memory budgets
.RB ( volumeMemoryMb ", " imageMemoryMb ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/slerp/file-types.jsonc
The choices made with
.B slerp associate
or the viewer's Settings, File Types.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/slerp/
What applying the choices changed outside Slerp, so it can be undone.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLERP_GPU
Overrides the
.B gpu
setting for one run.
.TP
.B SLERP_VIEWER_KEEP_ALIVE
Overrides
.BR viewerKeepAliveSeconds .
.TP
.BR SLERP_VOLUME_MEMORY_MB ", " SLERP_IMAGE_MEMORY_MB
Override
.B volumeMemoryMb
and
.BR imageMemoryMb .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dolphin (1),
.BR nautilus (1)
.PP
The README in
.I /usr/share/doc/slerp/
describes the viewer, the formats and the settings in full.
